#X text 82 5182 mgi (0): depth on the pitch in cents (83: 12.4 cents per step \, 186 at 15) \, a 14.5 Hz low-pass makes fast vibrato shallower \, as on the original. \; mgd (0): delay 0-15 (82: 0.47 s at 5 \, 1.55 s at 15) from the first key \, then full depth., f 64;
#X obj 460 5304 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 5280 6 0 15 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 5304 mgv \$1;
#X text 82 5334 mgv (0): MG to the VCF 0-15 (84: +-7.9 octaves at 15)., f 64;
#X obj 60 5384 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG4\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5418 A modulation envelope (not on the Poly-800) \, one for all voices like DEG3. The Poly-800 is paraphonic: every voice has its own DEG1 / DEG2 \, but the VCF \, DEG3 and the MG exist once - and so do DEG4 \, LFO2 and LFO3. Each of them has two target slots: t = target (number or name \, e.g. d4t1 cut) \, a = amount -127..127 (negative inverts). \; Targets (range at amount 127): 0 off \, 1 pitch (+-24 semitones) \, 2 pitch2 (DCO2 +-48) \, 3 detn (+-50 cents) \, 4 har1 \, 5 har2 (+-127 steps) \, 6 wsh1 \, 7 wsh2 (+-127) \, 8 wmx1 \, 9 wmx2 (+-127) \, 10 pw1 \, 11 pw2 (+-47 %) \, 12 fm1 \, 13 fm2 (+-16 index) \, 14 fmr (x/: 4) \, 15 ring (+-127) \, 16 swe (+-72 semitones) \, 17 lev1 \, 18 lev2 (+-127) \, 19 amp (level x 0..2 \, tremolo) \, 20 pan (balance) \, 21 nois (+-15) \, 22 cut (+-8 octaves) \, 23 res (+-15) \, 24 drv (+-127) \, 25 mgr (MG rate x/: 8) \, 26 mgi (+-200 cents) \, 27 l2r \, 29 l3r (LFO rate x/: 8) \, 28 l2d \, 30 l3d (LFO depth x 0..2) \, 31 dtim (delay time x/: 2) \, 32 dlev (+-15). har \, wsh \, wmx \, lev \, detn and drv follow per audio block \, smoothed by mrph \, all others per sample., f 64;
